# Extra files the source distribution must carry.
#
# NOTICE.md ships as a License-File and points readers at docs/sources.md for
# the Nordic references it relies on, so docs/ has to travel with it or the
# distributed legal text dangles. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md is the dependency
# license audit that docs/releasing.md reconciles at every tag, and examples/
# is what CI runs as its simulated smoke test — both belong next to the code
# they describe.
#
# `webui/` is deliberately absent. The sdist carries the *built* console in
# src/ppk2lab_web/static/, not the TypeScript it was built from: no Python build
# backend reads webui/, and rebuilding the bundle needs Node plus a node_modules
# tree an sdist cannot carry. Shipping the sources would invite a downstream
# packager to believe the bundle can be reproduced from the sdist, which it
# cannot. The sources are in the git repository; the licenses of everything
# compiled into the bundle are in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
include CHANGELOG.md
include CONTRIBUTING.md
include INSTALL.md
include NOTICE.md
include ROADMAP.md
include SECURITY.md
include THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
graft docs
graft examples
graft tests
